{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_uxdfpeeauz2raus6z3cqeqlka3t3a3byld2gu5h5idicaodhhnaq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four gate conditions hold.\n\n## Result: no behavioural divergence found\n\n`translation/src/lib.rs` needed **no changes** (mtime still `01:17`, untouched). The only two fixes were to my own test code. `Cargo.toml` gained only the requested `libloading` dev-dependency.\n\n## What was built\n\n**Phase A** — three artifacts derived mechanically from the C:\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — 4 exported symbols (`gotomach`, `process_value`, `double_value`, `triple_value`); the 4 `static` helpers and 3 macros correctly emit no symbols on either side.\n- `ERRORS.md` — **26 rows**, one per distinct rejection site found by grepping `lib.c` (both disjuncts of each range check separately, all six `result = -N` branches, both `init_processor` `return NULL`s, all three `cleanup:` NULL guards, both warning branches, plus FFI-boundary rows).\n- `CONFIGS.md` — **39 rows** across the axes the C actually branches on: `mode` × `iterations` shape × `seed` fold position × `threshold` append density × `count` saturation.\n\n**Phases B–D** — 79 tests, ~10M differential calls per run. Every test `dlopen`s **both** `.so`s and calls only exported symbols.\n\n## Two things worth calling out\n\n**Log bytes are compared, not just return values.** GCC lowers `printf(\"literal\\n\")` → `puts(...)`; LLVM does the same for the Rust, so both write through the same libc `stdout`. The harness taps fd 1 around each call and compares bytes exactly — this verifies `[INFO]`/`[WARNING]`/`[ERROR]` content *and ordering*. It required pinning libtest to one thread (`.cargo/config.toml`), since fd 1 is process-global.\n\n**Seven C builds, not one.** The C does signed `+`/`*` on `int` (formally UB) and reads a `malloc(0)` result. The Rust must match every *lowering*, not just one, so the matrix includes `gcc -O0/-O2/-O3/-Os` and `clang -O0/-O2` alongside the CMake default — 42 configurations, all green.\n\n## Honest caveats\n\n- **`ERRORS.md` rows 6–12 (`-3`/`-4`) and 9–10 (`-5`/`-6`) are unreachable through the FFI.** The API takes only `int`s, so the largest allocation is 256 KiB; `status` is unconditionally `1`; and `count <= i < iterations == capacity` makes `is_valid_state` always true. I assert the reachable half — both implementations *never* produce those sentinels (over a 50 000-case full-`i32` sweep and an exhaustive `iterations` 0..=512 append-everything sweep), and both treat `malloc(0)` and the 256 KiB maximum as success. Genuinely triggering them would need an allocator interposer.\n- **`--no-default-features` / `--all-features` are not independent code paths.** `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` table. Rather than assume, I confirmed the compiled test binary is byte-identical across all three combos (same SHA-256) — so I still ran all three, but they carry no extra information.\n- **The full matrix doesn't fit one 600 s command**, so `run_all.sh` takes a tier argument (`tier1`/`tier2a`/`tier2b`/`tier3a`/`tier3b`). I ran every tier; the last 12 debug-profile runs were driven directly because tier3 straddled the limit."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1157,"cache_read_input_tokens":159110,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1157,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"faa2ada5-a3a1-441c-980c-0b6a55393174","uuid":"56f67333-3fe2-44ec-abc1-f610236aa5b3","timestamp":"2026-08-28T02:48:08.791Z"}
